<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benedikt Kotruljević</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1416">1416</a>–<a href="/years/1469">1469</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Benedetto Cotrugli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benedikt Kotruljević (Benedetto Cotrugli) was a merchant, diplomat and writer from Ragusa (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubrovnik">Dubrovnik</a>) who served the Aragonese kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. His treatise on trade and the merchant's life, written in 1458 and printed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1573, contains one of the earliest known descriptions of double-entry bookkeeping, decades before Luca Pacioli's better-known account of 1494.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benedikt-kotruljevic.jpg" alt="Benedikt Kotruljević" width="320" height="519" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cotrugli, Benedetto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cotrugli_-_Della_mercatura,_1602_-_122.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
